NEARS-2816 delta re-QA (fix-cycle 1, commit 0f05cef1f), emulator-5562.

Fix landed: TB1 (hasVisibleScaffold() gate before consume, resolve against Get.context! instead
of HomeScreen's own context) + TB2 (DashboardScreen.initState + didPopNext call the function,
not just HomeScreen.initState, so a Profile-tab login that returns to the SAME Dashboard
instance still triggers it).

RE-VERIFIED CORRECT (the fix's own stated mechanism):
  - The Profile-tab login path (Sign In from profile_screen.dart, a pushed route on top of
    Dashboard) now DOES eventually consume the flag -- confirmed via
    flutter.6ammart_cart_merge_banner_pending going true->absent exactly when Dashboard's
    didPopNext fires (on the "Back" tap that pops profile_screen.dart back to Dashboard),
    matching the TB2 fix's documented mechanism. This was the ORIGINAL secondary finding
    (TB2) and IS now fixed at the consume-timing level.
  - No crash, no [FAIL]/[ERR], no red screen, in 2 independent trials.

STILL BROKEN (the actual visible symptom, i.e. AC1 itself):
Two independent live trials post-fix, using the SAME proxy-based repro technique validated in
the original QA pass (real guest cart + matched real guest_token for every guest-scoped call;
ONLY the login POST's guest_token field corrupted via a surgical reverse proxy 8010->8000):

  Trial A (guest_id=1405, backend rejects at [exact timestamp visible in laravel.log], banner
  triggered via DashboardScreen.initState on first Home landing after a Profile-tab login that
  returned to ProfileScreen, then "Back" to Dashboard triggering didPopNext): flag consumed,
  ZERO occurrences of "restore your saved cart items" across 8x 0.8s-spaced dumps immediately
  after the Back tap.

  Trial B (guest_id=1408, backend guest.cart.merge.rejected token_mismatch logged at
  2026-09-02 14:45:27, SAME Profile-tab -> Sign In -> Back -> didPopNext path): flag consumed
  (true -> absent) immediately after the "Back" tap, ZERO occurrences across 15x 0.6s-spaced
  dumps (~9s window) covering the didPopNext firing + the up-to-2.4s retry budget +
  the 2s display window. See paired bug-fix1-still-not-rendered-dump.xml (one representative
  dump of the 15, positive control: real content-desc nodes for Banana/Red Apples/Orange Juice
  present in the SAME dump, proving the accessibility instrument was live) and
  bug-fix1-still-not-rendered.png (screenshot, not read into QA's own context, saved as
  evidence only).

INTERPRETATION: since the flag is consumed only AFTER hasVisibleScaffold() returns true (per
the fix's own gating order), and it WAS consumed in both trials, hasVisibleScaffold() must have
returned true and NSnackBar.show(Get.context!, ...) must have been called -- yet the banner
still never became visible. This means the engineer's root-cause diagnosis (stale
HomeScreen-local context vs a non-current Scaffold) explains a REAL problem class but is
evidently NOT the (or not the only) reason this specific banner never renders live: routing
through Get.context! + the hasVisibleScaffold() gate did not change the observed symptom at
all. The defect is downstream of that fix -- possibly in NSnackBar/NToast's own rendering, or
in hasVisibleScaffold() itself returning a false-positive "visible" answer for a Scaffold that
is not actually the one painting on screen, or in Get.context resolving to something other than
the intuitively-expected Dashboard context at the moment didPopNext/initState fires. Not
diagnosed further live -- flagging precisely what WAS and was NOT confirmed so the next fix
cycle does not re-assume the TB1 diagnosis is complete.
